      "message": "it would be great if we could keep the sections here, as it was before.\n\nexample:\n\n    Getting Started\n    \u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n    .. toctree::\n        :maxdepth: 2\n\n        getting-started/index.rst\n\n\nrather than a single toc for everything.\n\nthe benefit of what I am proposing is we could add useful description about the docs being listed here. for example\n\n    Getting Started\n    \u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n\n    The documentation in this section provides guidance on how to get started with keystone, such as installing an upgrading, its architecture, ...\n\n    .. toctree::\n        :maxdepth: 2\n\n        getting-started/index.rst\n\nSo it looks more human-friendly rather than just a toc tree. I would like to see what others think about it too",
